2:T515,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does kitchen fitting take in Hemel Hempstead?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Timescales vary with the scope of work, the condition of the room, any layout changes and product availability. Ask the fitter for a project programme after the site survey and once the specification is known."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do kitchen fitters remove the old kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Many do, but it is not automatic. Check whether disconnection, removal, loading and waste disposal are included in the written quote."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should I buy the kitchen before contacting a fitter?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not necessarily. A fitter can often advise on measurements, layout and product compatibility before you order. This can help prevent problems with units, appliances and worktops."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is included in a kitchen fitting quote?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It may include cabinet installation, worktops, appliance fitting and basic preparation, but plumbing, electrics, tiling, flooring, decorating and waste disposal may be separate. Ask for a written itemised breakdown."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-fitters-hemel-hempstead","d"]
